WEBVTT

00:03.300 --> 00:05.095
Mac, you've got to
see this movie, dude.

00:05.216 --> 00:07.919
- Really? I found it boring.
- It's about the end of the world.

00:08.181 --> 00:09.885
Inconvenient Truth is not about that.

00:09.964 --> 00:11.924
It's about how,
if we don't stop global warming,

00:12.004 --> 00:15.116
- we're gonna destroy this environment.
- It sounds cool. I'll check it out.

00:15.169 --> 00:16.140
It's awesome.

00:17.676 --> 00:19.347
Dude, come on. What the hell is that?

00:19.796 --> 00:20.807
What?

00:21.173 --> 00:22.183
Are you kidding me?

00:23.114 --> 00:24.276
What is the big deal, Dennis?

00:24.356 --> 00:25.816
What is the big deal?
Are you nuts?

00:25.866 --> 00:28.231
You see a movie,
now you're crazy about the environment.

00:28.493 --> 00:31.327
I'm sorry. Maybe I would actually
like to do some good in this world.

00:31.393 --> 00:32.777
- Make a difference.
- You would?

00:33.178 --> 00:34.672
-You want to do good?
- Yes. I do.

00:34.738 --> 00:36.697
- You're not good at that.
- I can do good.

00:36.959 --> 00:38.324
I am capable of doing good.

00:38.586 --> 00:40.659
You just screw people over
for your own benefit.

00:40.731 --> 00:42.751
You guys are gonna be so angry
when you look back

00:42.801 --> 00:45.493
and see that the world looks
at Dennis Reynolds and says, "Dennis,

00:45.559 --> 00:48.155
"you are a good person,
you are making a dif... "

00:49.929 --> 00:51.003
Holy shit!

00:51.625 --> 00:52.630
What?

00:53.916 --> 00:55.240
There's a baby in
this Dumpster.

00:55.853 --> 00:58.642
Transcript: www.swsub.com

00:58.814 --> 01:01.681
Subtitles: Ju
www.top-series.net

01:31.740 --> 01:32.837
What the hell is it doing?

01:33.348 --> 01:36.389
- We got to call somebody.
- Who? The police?

01:36.495 --> 01:37.790
The mother?
I mean, think, Dee.

01:37.855 --> 01:40.942
Somebody threw this baby in the trash.
We can't put it back into the system.

01:40.992 --> 01:43.094
- It's a terrible system.
- It's a horrible system!

01:43.147 --> 01:46.137
We live in a throwaway culture.
Everyone's looking for the easy way out.

01:46.216 --> 01:48.775
Don't wanna carry your Big Gulp?
Just throw it in the street.

01:48.842 --> 01:51.492
Don't want to take care of your baby?
Throw it in a Dumpster.

01:51.553 --> 01:52.523
I just can't take it!

01:52.785 --> 01:54.700
- Charlie, you're harping on it!
- I'm sorry.

01:54.780 --> 01:57.442
I'd like to know whether or not
I share a bed with my father!

01:57.552 --> 01:59.862
I'm telling you,
I am not your father! Enough!

01:59.915 --> 02:02.711
- Then take a stupid blood test!
- I'm not taking no blood test!

02:02.817 --> 02:05.036
Look, I had enough of this,
I'm not even gonna talk...

02:05.550 --> 02:06.704
What the hell is that?

02:07.299 --> 02:09.316
It's a baby we found in the trash.

02:10.767 --> 02:12.460
Put it back.
It doesn't belong to you.

02:12.722 --> 02:14.086
We're not going to put it back.

02:14.348 --> 02:16.133
Give it to the cops.
Get it out of here.

02:16.199 --> 02:17.945
- It's bad for business.
- That's great.

02:18.019 --> 02:20.830
Pass the buck...
Everybody passing the buck, you know?

02:20.880 --> 02:23.763
It's time we start taking responsibility
for the refuse we're creating.

02:24.025 --> 02:25.049
Oh, my God, dude.

02:25.116 --> 02:27.642
Are you still harping on that
stupid global heating movie

02:27.904 --> 02:29.394
- you saw?
- Globalwarming, Charlie.

02:29.672 --> 02:31.208
Yeah, right.

02:31.447 --> 02:34.029
Like the Earth is magically
getting hotter.

02:34.285 --> 02:35.096
Stop!

02:35.162 --> 02:37.128
This is not the right
environment for a child.

02:37.178 --> 02:40.196
I'll take care of the baby until we
figure out what to do with it. Dee,

02:40.458 --> 02:42.157
- you're helping me.
- What? No, I'm not.

02:43.390 --> 02:45.677
See what's happening here?
Do you see this?

02:45.997 --> 02:48.318
Family values in this country
are going down the toilet.

02:48.368 --> 02:51.298
It's because of people like you.
Men and women raising a child together

02:51.377 --> 02:53.403
is a proven system
a thousand years old.

02:53.482 --> 02:55.882
There're parental roles
that need to be filled here, right?

02:56.015 --> 02:58.631
Otherwise, the kid winds up
roaming the streets, having

02:58.893 --> 03:01.175
unprotected sex
with multiple partners,

03:01.437 --> 03:02.927
sharing needles and contracting

03:03.189 --> 03:05.745
the HIV virus and it's all your fault.
Are you happy, Dee?

03:05.851 --> 03:08.698
Is this what you wanted? You just gave
this baby full-blown AIDS!

03:18.422 --> 03:20.314
What the hell are
these scrubs doing, dude?

03:20.364 --> 03:22.625
They're activists.
They're sifting through the trash

03:22.691 --> 03:24.425
looking for recyclable materials.

03:24.591 --> 03:26.409
Recycling? What a waste.

03:26.671 --> 03:29.780
Frank, we are trying
to make a difference.

03:31.718 --> 03:34.711
You see, he has no problem
not calling me "Dad."

03:36.301 --> 03:38.748
Uh, hey, man, where can I get
one of those recycle bags?

03:38.814 --> 03:40.241
Get lost, narc.

03:40.708 --> 03:41.716
Excuse me?

03:43.503 --> 03:45.167
What we're doing is
completely legal,

03:45.220 --> 03:46.947
you just leave us alone?

03:47.088 --> 03:49.098
I'm not a cop, man.
I just want to help out.

03:49.816 --> 03:52.285
Sure, you do. I saw you pull up
in that Range Rover.

03:52.377 --> 03:53.644
Is everything okay, Sage?

03:53.906 --> 03:56.589
No, everything is fine.
I was just explaing to your friend that

03:56.665 --> 03:58.232
- I wanna help you guys out.
- Listen,

03:58.494 --> 04:01.660
I know your type...
straight edge, mainline,

04:01.726 --> 04:04.536
weekend warrior coming
down here in your cashmere sweater,

04:04.629 --> 04:06.449
with your moussed-up,
hair-sprayed coif.

04:07.291 --> 04:09.118
This isn't just a hobby for us,

04:09.380 --> 04:12.641
so why don't you take your phony,
suburban, half-assed bullshit

04:12.891 --> 04:13.914
someplace else?

04:20.891 --> 04:22.767
I'll take that, hippie!

04:24.373 --> 04:25.677
Hey, Frank!

04:34.501 --> 04:36.382
Can you believe this thing, man?

04:39.647 --> 04:40.649
Charlie !

04:40.911 --> 04:42.368
Get down!

04:42.468 --> 04:43.856
This is amazing!
Look at this!

04:43.906 --> 04:46.614
You could chop a camel right in the hump
and drink all of its milk

04:46.667 --> 04:47.978
right off the tip of this thing!

04:48.058 --> 04:49.411
That is a find, man!

04:49.528 --> 04:51.243
- It's an Ali Baba sword!
- Spectacular!

04:51.928 --> 04:52.953
Let's get out of here.

04:53.216 --> 04:54.163
Look at this.

04:54.425 --> 04:57.465
I don't care about that, all right?
You're making me look like an asshole.

04:57.545 --> 05:00.340
I'm trying to make a difference,
and you're over here rummaging

05:00.432 --> 05:01.753
like a couple of narcs, okay?

05:01.846 --> 05:04.657
You can't just come down here
with your mainline, cashmere,

05:04.826 --> 05:09.204
moussed coif hairspray
and start being like a suburban tool!

05:12.304 --> 05:14.475
What are you saying?
Did you even look at this thing?

05:14.737 --> 05:17.506
I don't know. I think I just got
punk'd out by a couple of hippies.

05:18.592 --> 05:20.648
I got to do something about
this.

05:22.662 --> 05:24.265
God damn this dumbster baby's heavy!

05:24.345 --> 05:25.524
No, it's good for your back.

05:25.616 --> 05:28.318
All right, so we got the
diapers and the wipes and the
powder.

05:28.597 --> 05:30.074
Shit, this raising babies is easy.

05:31.420 --> 05:34.453
Okay, first things first. Baby smells
like trash. Throw it in the bath.

05:35.966 --> 05:37.619
- Already with this?
- I didn't do it.

05:37.670 --> 05:39.667
Already with this?
I come home to a crying baby?

05:40.074 --> 05:41.544
I didn't do anything. It's okay.

05:41.806 --> 05:43.501
You know what?
I'm just gonna kick back,

05:43.551 --> 05:45.047
grab a beer, and watch the Sixers.

05:45.309 --> 05:47.299
You're not gonna help me
and do this with you?

05:47.561 --> 05:49.590
Would it kill you to go shopping
once in a while?

05:49.696 --> 05:50.942
- We're out of beer.
- We are?

05:51.008 --> 05:53.055
We're not out of anything,
You don't live here.

05:53.780 --> 05:54.890
One left.

05:55.481 --> 05:57.242
If we're gonna raise
this baby together,

05:57.348 --> 05:59.986
I think it's important that we at
least try to make it work, so,

06:00.119 --> 06:03.006
when you're done with the bath,
why don't you go out and get some beer?

06:03.086 --> 06:05.088
And, um... a pack of smokes
would be good.

06:05.168 --> 06:07.369
We're not gonna raise anything
together. You know why?

06:07.419 --> 06:09.503
I said I would help you hang
onto this baby for

06:09.553 --> 06:11.841
a couple of days until
we figure out what to do with it.

06:11.877 --> 06:12.783
Really?

06:12.836 --> 06:14.851
- You're gonna raise your voice to me?
- I'm not.

06:14.901 --> 06:17.563
I'm trying to have a conversation,
I feel like you're berating me

06:17.613 --> 06:19.386
for absolutly no reason.
So, you know what?

06:19.485 --> 06:21.664
For the sake of the baby,
I think we need some space.

06:21.717 --> 06:23.966
I'm gonna go out with the guys
and blow off some steam.

06:24.016 --> 06:25.856
You're gonna dump
this thing on me and leave?

06:25.909 --> 06:28.465
You gonna guilt me into staying?
Okay, I guess I have to stay.

06:28.519 --> 06:29.737
For the sake of Dumpster baby.

06:29.817 --> 06:32.516
But I'll tell you what. I'm not gonna
stand here and be berated.

06:32.609 --> 06:33.739
I'm going to bed.

06:42.888 --> 06:43.898
Charlie!

06:44.177 --> 06:46.530
Would you just please lay there
and go to sleep?

06:46.676 --> 06:48.202
I can't sleep, dude. It's impossible.

06:48.252 --> 06:50.002
My mind's going like a mile a minute.

06:50.052 --> 06:52.201
Stop thinking about it.
I'm not your father.

06:52.254 --> 06:54.212
- Now, go to sleep.
- Dude, it's not that.

06:54.278 --> 06:56.887
I'm thinking about something
completely different.

06:57.775 --> 07:00.915
- It's the trash, isn't it?
- It's the sweet, sweet trash.

07:01.364 --> 07:03.684
I mean, man, we found some
amazing shit out there, today.

07:03.734 --> 07:06.587
The kind of shit I didn't think
you could find in the trash, you know?

07:06.919 --> 07:09.978
I'm just going nuts thinking
about what else is out there.

07:10.058 --> 07:12.072
Frank, there's ordinary guys
just like you and me

07:12.122 --> 07:13.892
going through everyone else's trash.

07:13.942 --> 07:16.112
People don't appreciate
their trash, Frank.

07:19.236 --> 07:21.056
Let's go get the flashlights.

07:24.074 --> 07:27.109
So I scale this tree.
This is a big tree, too, right?

07:27.162 --> 07:30.263
I get to the top of it, I find
the nest. This is baby bluebirds.

07:30.726 --> 07:33.531
They're starving to death, so I
regurgitate my lunch

07:34.440 --> 07:36.367
nourish the entire flock...

07:36.629 --> 07:40.016
Well, well, well,
check it out, babe, the narc is back.

07:40.956 --> 07:42.206
Hey, uh, Sage,

07:42.468 --> 07:44.074
I thought about what you said and

07:44.180 --> 07:46.511
I think you were right, man,
I was half-assing it,

07:46.603 --> 07:48.381
but I'm not gonna half-ass it anymore.

07:48.762 --> 07:51.423
I'm gonna devote myself
completely to the cause.

07:51.685 --> 07:54.459
Look, bro, just 'cause you come
in here with your Birkenstocks

07:54.512 --> 07:56.810
and your Phish T- shirt
doesn't mean you're devoted.

07:57.009 --> 07:58.389
It means you're a total poser.

07:59.989 --> 08:01.570
Wow, um...

08:02.577 --> 08:05.213
You know what, man?
I'm just gonna go, then, I guess.

08:05.405 --> 08:08.306
You know, I'll take my Birkenstocks
and my Phish T- shirt

08:08.749 --> 08:11.694
- and my kine bud with me.
- What?

08:13.378 --> 08:15.418
Did you just say you had kine bud?

08:15.692 --> 08:19.004
Kine bu... Yeah, I mean, you know,
I just have, like,

08:20.010 --> 08:21.626
this much.

08:22.850 --> 08:26.440
- Look at this, a little ray gun, like.
- That's nice!

08:26.519 --> 08:28.241
Look at this thing right here, dude.

08:28.334 --> 08:31.399
Put this in a plastic bag and boom!
Shower radio, buddy.

08:32.685 --> 08:35.259
- Unbelievable.
- Look at this.

08:35.485 --> 08:37.365
We wrap stuff in this.

08:37.551 --> 08:39.763
Look... wrap it all up.

08:41.094 --> 08:43.225
Electrics? Electrics!

08:46.055 --> 08:47.525
- &A sneaker!
- What size?

08:47.617 --> 08:49.815
- 14.
- Throw it in the pile, baby.

08:50.197 --> 08:51.377
Right in the pile.

08:51.482 --> 08:53.415
Oh, Charlie, isn't this great?

08:53.588 --> 08:55.779
We go right to the source,
forget about the dump.

08:56.041 --> 08:58.667
Yeah, screw the dump, man.
It's right in your backyard, dude.

08:58.720 --> 08:59.876
This is it.

09:00.018 --> 09:02.328
- What's that? What's that?
- It's another coat, man!

09:02.590 --> 09:04.349
- Ooh, can I have it?
- No.

09:04.534 --> 09:06.481
- You already got one.
- Frank, use your head.

09:06.534 --> 09:08.662
This is the coat that's gonna
protect my other coat.

09:08.743 --> 09:09.752
Come on, man.

09:11.633 --> 09:14.560
- When you're right, you're right.
- Yeah, baby, you'll find one.

09:14.653 --> 09:16.970
If you keep digging, you're
gonna find one of these.

09:17.050 --> 09:18.878
Oh, you gotta be kidding me.

09:18.931 --> 09:20.346
Oh, hello.

09:20.872 --> 09:22.422
Look who it is, huh?

09:22.687 --> 09:26.091
The girl who ruined my life,
by falling in love with my best friend

09:26.170 --> 09:28.297
and having sex
with this guy right here.

09:28.429 --> 09:30.105
- How you doin'?
- Gross,

09:30.367 --> 09:32.972
and gross to you. You know what?
I don't know what you're doing.

09:33.091 --> 09:35.402
I don't want to know.
Do it in somebody else's Dumpster.

09:37.054 --> 09:39.239
Hold on a second.
What do you got in those?

09:40.089 --> 09:41.741
Coffee cups and food scraps.

09:42.976 --> 09:44.995
- Yeah, we'll take 'em.
- Hand 'em over.

09:46.967 --> 09:49.538
- I don't know why it's cranky.
- Maybe he's hungry, all right?

09:49.596 --> 09:51.716
- Should we nursing it?
- I haven't slept in 3 days.

09:51.782 --> 09:53.425
I don't have any thoughts anymore.

09:53.703 --> 09:56.086
Raising a child is not nearly as fun
as I thought it'd be.

09:56.206 --> 09:59.218
Well, what if we put it back
where we found it?

10:04.050 --> 10:08.315
Oh, my God, that is the cutest
little baby I've ever seen.

10:08.391 --> 10:09.395
What's his name?

10:10.342 --> 10:12.461
- Uh, his name?
- It's...

10:12.693 --> 10:14.316
- D.B.
- D.B.

10:15.569 --> 10:17.741
Oh, he could be a Gerber baby.

10:17.807 --> 10:19.501
He could be in commercials.

10:23.052 --> 10:25.609
- I have an idea.
- I'm three steps ahead of you.

10:25.662 --> 10:27.996
- We need to make Dumpster baby a star.
- Exactly.

10:28.258 --> 10:31.402
This is what I'm talking about. We can't
put it back into a corrupt system.

10:31.508 --> 10:33.335
We have an opportunity
to give it a future.

10:33.597 --> 10:34.888
Yes, by making it a star.

10:35.224 --> 10:37.076
And who have better
lives than child stars?

10:37.126 --> 10:39.091
- Nobody.
- Rich, famous, they have it all.

10:39.353 --> 10:41.121
They're the happiest people on hearth.

10:41.478 --> 10:44.789
D.B, my main man, you got tossed
into the right Dumpster.

10:49.947 --> 10:52.617
Brenda, I'm not gonna waste any more
of your time than I have to.

10:52.679 --> 10:55.315
We've got meetings with agents
all over town.

10:55.474 --> 10:57.025
Can you make D.B. a star?

10:57.501 --> 11:00.968
Well, I'm sorry to say,
but in today's commercial world,

11:01.061 --> 11:03.666
there's just no room for
another white baby actor.

11:03.812 --> 11:05.117
There's an influx already.

11:05.449 --> 11:06.493
White babies don't sell.

11:06.755 --> 11:08.282
White babies aren't selling right now.

11:08.352 --> 11:10.122
Question: who is selling, Brenda?

11:10.384 --> 11:13.751
Well, the Latino market is the fastest
growing demographic in the country.

11:14.013 --> 11:16.887
- Great. So Mexicans are selling.
- Oh, well, D.B. can play Mexican.

11:16.937 --> 11:18.380
D.B. could definitely be a Mexican.

11:18.699 --> 11:19.923
We get him some pistols.

11:20.185 --> 11:22.542
He fires 'em off like crazy.
Do the jumping thing.

11:22.635 --> 11:24.553
He does the Mexican jumping bean.

11:26.720 --> 11:28.777
We get him a little thing
with the chips.

11:28.870 --> 11:30.837
And he can dip the chips
into the nacho cheese.

11:30.930 --> 11:32.426
- It's perfect.
- It's hilarious.

11:32.559 --> 11:34.062
For all we know, he is Mexican.

11:34.515 --> 11:36.877
- 'Cause here's the thing.
- Oh, oh, we got...

11:37.040 --> 11:39.400
I can't really get into the specifics
of the whole thing,

11:39.450 --> 11:41.096
but we've got no idea
who D.B.'s dad is.

11:41.146 --> 11:43.197
We don't know who the dad is.
It isn't me...

11:43.809 --> 11:47.117
Sorry, but your son
just does not look Latino.

11:47.379 --> 11:50.799
Oh, well, I mean, that's a bit of a...

11:50.849 --> 11:52.691
- disappointment for us.
- That makes me sad.

11:52.744 --> 11:55.563
Because we're truly trying
to give him a future.

11:55.656 --> 11:56.960
Is there anything we can do?

11:57.762 --> 12:01.131
Not unless you can change
the color of this baby's skin.

12:03.785 --> 12:05.010
Let me get this straight.

12:05.272 --> 12:07.846
You want to put your baby
into a tanning bed?

12:08.257 --> 12:11.521
- That's correct.
- I'm sorry, that's against the law.

12:11.680 --> 12:13.911
Look, pal, we are well
aware of the law, okay?

12:13.961 --> 12:15.262
We don't want to jam you up.

12:15.312 --> 12:17.789
We just want to put him in there
for a couple of minutes.

12:17.908 --> 12:18.954
Just to get a base.

12:19.007 --> 12:21.207
We'll sign whatever waivers
or whatever you need.

12:21.260 --> 12:23.237
Let us cook him,
and we'll be out of your hair.

12:23.499 --> 12:25.864
I'm feeling compelled to call
the authorities.

12:26.126 --> 12:29.235
Oh, are you? Then why don't we take
our business elsewhere?

12:29.314 --> 12:32.135
I sense some judgment in your voice,
sir, and I don't appreciate it.

12:32.207 --> 12:34.498
You could have help change
this child's life forever.

12:34.551 --> 12:36.405
You chose not to.
That's on you.

12:36.498 --> 12:37.942
I can live with that.

12:38.088 --> 12:39.240
Come on, D.B.

12:39.492 --> 12:43.000
I guess the road to stardom is paved
with hard knocks and orange assholes.

12:45.145 --> 12:46.753
Trees are people, too!

12:46.912 --> 12:48.053
Save this tree!

12:48.315 --> 12:51.667
These developer pigs
are gonna tear down this tree.

12:51.750 --> 12:54.393
So tonight, we will hold
a candlelight vigil

12:54.655 --> 12:55.667
in protest.

12:56.170 --> 12:58.552
Sage, Asrael,
can we commune for a moment?

12:58.602 --> 12:59.609
Yeah, what's up?

12:59.675 --> 13:02.245
Listen, I don't want to be
putting out any negative vibrations

13:02.325 --> 13:05.529
or anything like that, but I think we're
going about this the wrong way.

13:05.791 --> 13:07.138
Thanks, but we got it.

13:07.204 --> 13:08.949
Why don't we hear him out, Sage?

13:09.718 --> 13:11.185
Thanks, Asrael.

13:11.360 --> 13:14.261
Well, listen, while I think
lighting a couple of candles

13:14.327 --> 13:16.984
and singing a few sweet jams
sounds like a really good time,

13:17.236 --> 13:18.876
it's not gonna stop a bulldozer.

13:19.354 --> 13:22.546
Somebody needs to step up and be
a hero here. So I'm thinking,

13:22.808 --> 13:24.667
I would chain myself to that tree,

13:25.250 --> 13:29.303
and that way, if they want to kill
that tree, they got to kill me first.

13:30.005 --> 13:31.722
That is so brave of
you, Dennis.

13:32.098 --> 13:33.376
- Is it?
- Wait.

13:33.831 --> 13:37.460
If anyone is gonna chain themselves
to anything, it's gonna be me.

13:37.526 --> 13:40.314
- But it was Dennis' idea.
- No, wait, Asrael, he's right.

13:40.950 --> 13:41.982
Maybe it should be him.

13:42.244 --> 13:43.942
Right, I'm the one in charge here.

13:44.204 --> 13:45.569
You're the one in charge.

13:46.223 --> 13:48.280
- Right, Mountain, go get some chains.
- No, wait.

13:48.542 --> 13:50.491
hold off on that, Mountain.

13:51.569 --> 13:52.811
I brought some.

13:53.940 --> 13:55.707
Charlie, we gotta stop, we gotta stop.

13:55.757 --> 13:58.652
- Two more, let's keep it moving.
- We gotta drop off at the base camp.

13:58.731 --> 14:00.876
No, no, base camp.
We got to keep moving.

14:02.870 --> 14:05.556
Do not lose that! Do not lose that!

14:05.874 --> 14:08.091
I think we gotta stop.
We gotta stop at the apartment.

14:08.417 --> 14:11.079
- No, dude, no time for that, man.
- We gotta drop some stuff.

14:11.146 --> 14:12.721
All right, fine. Well, make it quick.

14:12.893 --> 14:13.965
All right.

14:16.006 --> 14:18.268
Charlie, maybe we should get rid
of some of this shit.

14:18.374 --> 14:20.440
- What?
- Yeah.

14:20.586 --> 14:22.505
- What'd you say, get rid of it?
- Yeah.

14:23.896 --> 14:25.911
Frank, look at this. Huh?

14:26.136 --> 14:28.612
This-This... look at that, bro.

14:29.050 --> 14:30.663
This shit is our future, man.

14:30.743 --> 14:32.981
People are throwing this away.
Get rid of it, dude?

14:33.100 --> 14:34.551
Frank, we start getting rid of this,

14:34.630 --> 14:36.657
we're gonna just like
the wasters out there.

14:37.359 --> 14:39.309
Guess what?
Somebody else is gonna find it.

14:39.389 --> 14:41.124
You're right, you're right.

14:41.386 --> 14:42.709
Where are we gonna sleep?

14:50.654 --> 14:52.230
So you still want to do this?

14:52.813 --> 14:55.297
Mountain, this is what
it's all about.

14:55.713 --> 14:59.450
Me and my girl, side by side,
saving a life,

15:00.033 --> 15:02.521
bringing in the dawn together.
I mean, come on.

15:03.742 --> 15:06.586
- Looks like it's gonna rain.
- It does look like it's gonna rain.

15:06.785 --> 15:07.818
Have you seen Asrael?

15:08.653 --> 15:09.672
No.

15:11.007 --> 15:12.861
Wonder where she is.

15:18.235 --> 15:20.827
Tonight, we cross the plane of reality

15:20.946 --> 15:23.738
into the dimension
of no place or time.

15:24.841 --> 15:26.189
Open your mouth.

15:29.027 --> 15:31.331
Become the journey.

15:34.773 --> 15:36.160
What are we doing, man?

15:36.319 --> 15:37.639
It's pouring rain out here!

15:38.177 --> 15:40.814
- We're like animals.
- Look, we got to stick together,

15:40.887 --> 15:42.596
- we gonna make it.
- We stick together.

15:42.663 --> 15:44.994
- All right, let's use our heads.
- What are we gonna do?

15:45.073 --> 15:46.795
- We got to get off of this rain.
- Yeah.

15:46.901 --> 15:48.226
Where are we gonna go?

15:50.775 --> 15:52.154
We could get in that Dumpster.

15:53.941 --> 15:55.991
I'm not above that.
Let's go.

15:56.418 --> 15:58.063
Asrael!

15:59.651 --> 16:01.484
Where are you?!

16:22.279 --> 16:24.050
- Can I get a bite of that, dude?
- Okay.

16:24.171 --> 16:25.773
I'm starving.

16:26.806 --> 16:29.769
Charlie, I'm really sorry
that I banged your girlfriend.

16:29.848 --> 16:31.967
Bro, you got to stop talking
about that, dude.

16:32.073 --> 16:34.158
I'm also sorry that I
didn't get the blood test.

16:34.264 --> 16:37.724
But I know I'm a hundred percent
positive that I am not your dad.

16:38.008 --> 16:39.762
How can you be
a hundred percent positive?

16:39.868 --> 16:41.034
How do you know?

16:41.497 --> 16:44.398
Your mother and I were gonna
keep this a secret, but...

16:45.949 --> 16:48.465
After we made love,
she did get pregnant.

16:48.994 --> 16:50.522
But she had an abortion.

16:51.908 --> 16:53.524
- Really?
- Yeah. Yeah.

16:54.703 --> 16:56.634
Are you sure
she went through with it, dude?

16:56.753 --> 16:57.926
Maybe she didn't tell you.

16:58.014 --> 17:00.455
She probably went right from the clinic,
banged some guy

17:00.548 --> 17:03.725
and got knocked up,
because your mother was a giant whore.

17:04.177 --> 17:06.350
You know what, dude?
I don't believe you, Frank.

17:06.403 --> 17:08.939
- It's hard to take.
- Oh, my God. You're a liar, man.

17:13.619 --> 17:15.103
Where are you going,
Charlie?!

17:15.182 --> 17:16.761
To find out the
truth!

17:18.639 --> 17:20.175
Charlie!

17:32.188 --> 17:35.014
- Frank doesn't know the truth.
- I knew it.

17:35.081 --> 17:37.894
All right, you didn't have an abortion,
you just told him you did.

17:37.960 --> 17:39.344
- I get that.
- No.

17:39.606 --> 17:42.135
I had an abortion,
it just didn't take.

17:44.267 --> 17:45.642
What does that mean?

17:46.015 --> 17:48.439
It means you survived it.

17:48.670 --> 17:50.816
You survived the abortion.

17:51.717 --> 17:53.558
What the hell
are you talking about, Ma?

17:53.624 --> 17:57.099
We went to one of those clinics,
one of those underground clinics

17:57.179 --> 17:59.311
because Frank didn't want
to spend a lot of money.

17:59.453 --> 18:03.090
And I had the procedure
and then they told me you were dead.

18:03.448 --> 18:07.112
And then, three month later,
you popped out, happy as a clam.

18:08.477 --> 18:11.126
Sweetie, I had to keep it a
secret from Frank.

18:11.508 --> 18:13.853
I never wanted the abortion
in the first place.

18:13.946 --> 18:15.297
But he was married,

18:15.559 --> 18:18.300
I knew if he found out,
he would've forced me to get rid of you,

18:18.562 --> 18:20.015
once and for all.

18:20.664 --> 18:23.778
He would've made me
throw you in a Dumpster.

18:26.978 --> 18:31.058
Oh... my... God.

18:33.321 --> 18:35.525
- No, his skin need to be darker, Dee.
- Yeah, I know.

18:35.787 --> 18:37.839
We're just gonna paint
this bronzing lotion on him

18:37.905 --> 18:39.512
- Shoe polish.
- Shoe polish?

18:39.605 --> 18:41.602
Shoe polish on a baby?
You are such an idiot.

18:41.695 --> 18:43.350
Gonna look stupid and smell like shit.

18:43.470 --> 18:44.563
We'll see.

18:45.205 --> 18:46.379
Where's D.B ?

18:46.655 --> 18:47.751
My door's open.

18:48.527 --> 18:50.329
- Did he get kidnapped?
- Somebody took him?

18:50.395 --> 18:51.640
There's a note.

18:52.594 --> 18:53.600
"Taked baby.

18:53.693 --> 18:56.142
"Meet at later bar,
night or day sometime."

18:57.875 --> 18:58.875
Charlie.

18:59.186 --> 19:02.093
Feast your eyes on this.

19:02.355 --> 19:04.353
Oh, my God, Charlie,
where did you get a baby?

19:04.459 --> 19:07.227
I think you know good and well
where I got this baby now, don't you?

19:07.320 --> 19:11.041
- What the hell are you talking about?
- I'm talking about you and Frank

19:11.213 --> 19:13.981
throwing your love child here
in the Dumpster behind Paddy's Pub.

19:14.061 --> 19:15.421
Do you think I wouldn't find out?

19:15.501 --> 19:17.328
Well, I did, yeah.

19:17.408 --> 19:19.858
What you might not know,
is that this little baby of yours

19:19.911 --> 19:21.780
also happens to be my half brother.

19:22.520 --> 19:25.368
Charlie, the incident with Frank
happened three months ago.

19:25.474 --> 19:27.029
It takes nine months to make a baby.

19:27.097 --> 19:29.454
So you can just give me the baby
and stop screaming.

19:29.716 --> 19:31.442
There was time
where I would've helped you

19:31.521 --> 19:33.932
raise this little Dumpster baby
brother of mine like a son,

19:33.998 --> 19:36.055
that's gone now 'cause you ruined it!

19:36.307 --> 19:37.999
You threw your babies away!

19:38.296 --> 19:39.965
And you threw your swords away!

19:40.336 --> 19:42.467
You threw your golf clubs and
your tasty treats!

19:42.892 --> 19:45.024
And you know what? I found them.

19:45.197 --> 19:46.638
And I'm gonna raise all of them.

19:48.044 --> 19:49.795
Get me the number for Child Services.

19:54.497 --> 19:57.065
Sage, buddy, how are you, man?
How're you feeling?

19:57.327 --> 19:59.875
I did it. I saved the tree.

20:00.237 --> 20:01.403
You sure did, man.

20:01.919 --> 20:03.111
You saved that tree.

20:03.403 --> 20:04.959
I got to say, I'm really impressed.

20:05.052 --> 20:06.715
I could've done
what you did here today.

20:06.794 --> 20:09.748
- I'm a hero.
- You are, you're a hero. Come here.

20:09.913 --> 20:11.238
Come here, come with me.

20:11.397 --> 20:12.889
Man, it is a good day to be alive.

20:12.939 --> 20:14.710
It's a good day to be alive, isn't it?

20:16.286 --> 20:18.698
Okay, guys, she's all yours.

20:23.440 --> 20:24.718
You might want to see this.

20:32.919 --> 20:34.336
I banged your girlfriend.

20:35.515 --> 20:37.382
What time did he say he
was gonna meet us?

20:37.449 --> 20:39.115
"Later bar, night or day sometime."

20:39.208 --> 20:40.771
- What does that mean?
- I don't know.

20:40.824 --> 20:43.611
Hey, any of you guys seen
that Ali Baba sword that Charlie had?

20:44.430 --> 20:45.701
- What?
- The little shit

20:45.767 --> 20:48.350
dumped me in a Dumpster, last night.
I'm taking all the stuff.

20:48.403 --> 20:49.492
Every man for himself.

20:49.966 --> 20:51.529
I got to fing another Baba sword.

20:51.662 --> 20:54.331
Pour me a shot there, I am the man.

20:54.637 --> 20:56.227
Why are you so chipper?

20:56.306 --> 20:58.001
I got punked out
by this peace activist.

20:58.353 --> 21:00.817
So what I did is,
I infiltrated his organization,

21:00.910 --> 21:02.763
- I banged his girlfriend...
- Hey, Frank!

21:03.191 --> 21:05.550
You recognize this young man
right here?

21:05.946 --> 21:07.986
Or should I say "Hey, Dad"?

21:08.856 --> 21:10.246
That's right, everybody.

21:10.365 --> 21:12.922
Who would like to hear
a mind-blowing story?

21:13.028 --> 21:15.184
Nobody. Give us back our baby,
so we can paint it.

21:15.258 --> 21:17.242
You're gonna paint it?
Be careful painting it

21:17.335 --> 21:19.217
'cause you'll be painting my brother.

21:19.323 --> 21:21.358
I guess you already knew that,
didn't you, Dad?

21:21.934 --> 21:23.485
What the hell are you talking about?

21:23.908 --> 21:26.570
About you and the waitress
duming your baby in a Dumpster.

21:27.054 --> 21:29.305
And the abortion that you tried
to make my mom have.

21:29.371 --> 21:31.612
Well, guess what, Frankie?
It didn't take.

21:31.718 --> 21:33.546
I'm an abortion survivor, Dad!

21:33.652 --> 21:35.955
- I survived the abortion, Dad!
- First of all,

21:36.480 --> 21:38.797
it takes nine months to have a baby.

21:38.917 --> 21:40.460
That is not my baby.

21:41.147 --> 21:44.756
Second of all, your mother is
feeding you a line of crap.

21:45.480 --> 21:47.299
Holy shit, you guys kept
the Ali Baba sword?

21:47.365 --> 21:49.233
Gimme the sword.
That's the sword, I want it.

21:49.300 --> 21:50.399
Back off, man.

21:51.191 --> 21:53.306
- I'm trying to play with it.
- It's my sword.

22:06.363 --> 22:08.283
